course: dictionary
lesson: 4779
title: Reading feelings in how people speak
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a character feels, even when the character does not say so. Huffily is one of these. When someone does something huffily, they are sulky, annoyed and offended, because their feelings or pride have been hurt. In Alice's story, the Dormouse grumbles that Alice is growing in his space, and then he answers huffily that he grows «at a reasonable pace», and moves away.
explain: Look at what happens around the word. Is the character offended? Do they sulk, turn away or walk off? These clues show that huffily means sulky and hurt, not happy or excited. Always ask: would a cheerful person behave like this? If not, the word is probably about bad feelings.
explain: Huffily is an adverb. Adverbs tell you how something is done, so huffily tells you how a character speaks or moves. Try the swap test: put a word with the same meaning, such as sulkily, into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have worked out the meaning.
fact: Huffily means in a sulky, annoyed and offended way.
fact: Huffily is an adverb, so it tells how someone speaks or moves.
fact: «Said huffily» and «walked off huffily» show a character whose pride is hurt.
fact: Huffily is about sulking and feeling offended, so it does not mean loud or shouting.
fact: In Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, many creatures take offence and answer huffily.
exercise: The Dormouse says huffily that he grows «at a reasonable pace», and moves away. What does huffily mean? | In a very quiet whisper | In a happy and excited way | *In a sulky, annoyed and offended way | In a hurry to finish
exercise: «He walked off huffily.» Find and copy the word that tells how he walked off. | he | off | walked | *huffily
exercise: «She shut the door huffily and sat in silence.» Which feeling does huffily show? | Frightened of the dark | Bored and sleepy | Joyful and excited | *Sulky and offended
test: Ben says, «I'm not talking to you», and turns away huffily. What does huffily tell us about Ben? | Ben is running to catch the bus | Ben is lost and scared | Ben is laughing at a funny joke | *Ben is sulking because his pride is hurt
test: «Mia answered huffily.» Which word could swap in for huffily and keep the same meaning? | *sulkily | happily | quietly | quickly
exam: Which is the best meaning of huffily? | Quick and eager | Happy and excited | Very tired after a long walk | *Sulky, annoyed and offended, with hurt pride
